  "notes": [
    "EBIT is not presented as a standalone line item in the filing; EBIT in this package is computed as (Income from continuing operations before income taxes + Interest and other financial charges) to approximate earnings before interest and taxes. ([sec.gov](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/40545/000004054526000008/ge-20251231.htm))",
    "D&A is modeled as (Depreciation and amortization of property, plant and equipment + Amortization of intangible assets) taken from the Statement of Cash Flows (excluding goodwill impairments). ([sec.gov](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/40545/000004054526000008/ge-20251231.htm))",
    "Capex is modeled using gross cash additions to property, plant and equipment and internal-use software (not net of dispositions). ([sec.gov](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/40545/000004054526000008/ge-20251231.htm))",
    "NWC is constructed from the balance sheet as: (Current assets \u2212 cash, cash equivalents & restricted cash \u2212 current investment securities) \u2212 (Current liabilities \u2212 short-term borrowings). This yields negative NWC for GE in the historical period due to GE\u2019s balance-sheet working capital structure. ([sec.gov](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/40545/000004054526000008/ge-20251231.htm))",
    "Tax rate uses GAAP effective income tax rate of 14.1% for FY2025 as the base-case tax_rate. ([sec.gov](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/40545/000004054526000008/ge-20251231.htm))",
    "WACC is a model estimate using: risk-free rate from FRED (10-year DGS10), equity beta from GuruFocus, and an equity risk premium assumption of 0.05; cost of debt is approximated from interest and other financial charges divided by average total borrowings, after tax. ([fred.stlouisfed.org](https://fred.stlouisfed.org/series/DGS10))",
    "NOL balance is set to null because the filing provides loss-carryforward information primarily in the context of deferred tax assets (tax-effected amounts) and valuation allowances, not an explicit NOL dollars balance suitable for direct utilization modeling. ([sec.gov](https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/40545/000004054526000008/ge-20251231.htm))",
    "Investments is set to null because the package requires a single 'investments' scalar for the DCF equity bridge, but the filing discloses multiple investment categories (e.g., equity investments, insurance investment securities, equity method investments) that are not consistently convertible into one scalar without additional model conventions."
  ],
